\newlabel{fig:greennonpoint}{{5.3}{223}{Representation of the Green's functions for non-point sources. Under these boundary conditions the Green's functions still behave as mirror images, but now with given volume and geometry; the only constraint on the emission of these sources is that, on the boundary $z=0$, the total field must vanish, as required by the assumed Dirichlet conditions}{figure.caption.65}{}}
