\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.6}{\ignorespaces The two cardinal spheres of radius $R$ associated with a propagation over the distance $z$. The emitting cap $\mathcal  {A}$ is tangent to its plane at $V_{\mathcal  {A}}$ with its centre of curvature downstream at $C_{\mathcal  {A}}$, of abscissa $R$, and the receiving cap $\mathcal  {B}$ is tangent to its plane at $V_{\mathcal  {B}}$ with its centre upstream at $C_{\mathcal  {B}}$, of abscissa $z-R$, so that the two caps bow towards each other. The quantity $\delta $ is the sagitta \eqref  {eq:FrFT:Sagitta}. The confocal case of Figure~\ref {fig:ConfocalSpheres} is recovered when $R = z$, since then $C_{\mathcal  {A}}$ falls on $V_{\mathcal  {B}}$ and $C_{\mathcal  {B}}$ on $V_{\mathcal  {A}}$.}}{252}{figure.caption.68}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:CardinalSpheres}{{5.6}{252}{The two cardinal spheres of radius $R$ associated with a propagation over the distance $z$. The emitting cap $\mathcal {A}$ is tangent to its plane at $V_{\mathcal {A}}$ with its centre of curvature downstream at $C_{\mathcal {A}}$, of abscissa $R$, and the receiving cap $\mathcal {B}$ is tangent to its plane at $V_{\mathcal {B}}$ with its centre upstream at $C_{\mathcal {B}}$, of abscissa $z-R$, so that the two caps bow towards each other. The quantity $\delta $ is the sagitta \eqref {eq:FrFT:Sagitta}. The confocal case of Figure~\ref {fig:ConfocalSpheres} is recovered when $R = z$, since then $C_{\mathcal {A}}$ falls on $V_{\mathcal {B}}$ and $C_{\mathcal {B}}$ on $V_{\mathcal {A}}$}{figure.caption.68}{}}
